1541</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Ikonen, E., M. Tagaya, O. Ullrich, C. Montecucco, and K. Simons. <year>1995</year>. Different requirements for NSF, SNAP, and Rab proteins in apical and basolateral transport in MDCK cells. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>81</volume>:<fpage>571</fpage>&#x02013;580.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7758111</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Jahn, R., and R.H. Scheller. <year>2006</year>. SNAREs&#x02014;engines for membrane fusion. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>631</fpage>&#x02013;643.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16912714</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Kreitzer, G., J. Schmoranzer, S.H. Low, X. Li, Y. Gan, T. Weimbs, S.M. Simon, and E. Rodriguez-Boulan. <year>2003</year>. Three-dimensional analysis of post-Golgi carrier exocytosis in epithelial cells. <source>Nat. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>5</volume>:<fpage>126</fpage>&#x02013;136.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12545172</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Lafont, F., P. Verkade, T. Galli, C. Wimmer, D. Louvard, and K. Simons. <year>1999</year>. Raft association of SNAP receptors acting in apical trafficking in Madin-Darby canine kidney cells. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>96</volume>:<fpage>3734</fpage>&#x02013;3738.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10097106</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Li, X., S.H. Low, M. Miura, and T. Weimbs. <year>2002</year>. SNARE expression and localization in renal epithelial cells suggest mechanism for variability of trafficking phenotypes. <source>Am. J. Physiol. Renal Physiol.</source> <volume>283</volume>:<fpage>F1111</fpage>&#x02013;F1122.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12372788</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Low, S.H., S.J. Chapin, T. Weimbs, L.G. Komuves, M.K. B